{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39659740",
      "title": "You Don't Have To Use JSX!",
      "sourceHash": "0e4ae28dedac2799b30bf0147d2ac4f2b5e04c6729af2e4b77037fb6443f8982",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "Now we'll get started in this section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 7.65,
          "en": "by taking another look at this JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.65,
          "end": 11.88,
          "en": "this HTML in JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.88,
          "end": 15.003,
          "en": "about which you learned in the last course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.9,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "Because there I mentioned that this JSX code, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 23.01,
          "en": "is a non-standard feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.01,
          "end": 25.59,
          "en": "It's not supported by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.59,
          "end": 29.7,
          "en": "and therefore the code you write in your code files here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 29.7,
          "end": 33.9,
          "en": "is not the code that ends up in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.9,
          "end": 36.9,
          "en": "Instead, as you learned, we got a build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.9,
          "end": 41.19,
          "en": "that's running behind the scenes that actually transforms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.19,
          "end": 44.58,
          "en": "and potentially also optimizes our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.58,
          "end": 47.85,
          "en": "such that it does work in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.85,
          "end": 50.04,
          "en": "But as a React developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.04,
          "end": 53.13,
          "en": "you should know that, in theory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.13,
          "end": 57.36,
          "en": "you could also build React apps without using JSX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.36,
          "end": 59.73,
          "en": "and therefore, if you needed to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.73,
          "end": 64.08,
          "en": "without using such a build process, though I will also say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.08,
          "end": 67.92,
          "en": "that the vast majority of React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.92,
          "end": 70.71000000000001,
          "en": "will use this JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.71000000000001,
          "end": 73.68,
          "en": "and a build process that transforms it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.68,
          "end": 75.42,
          "en": "And that will also be the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.42,
          "end": 77.73,
          "en": "for all the projects in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.73,
          "end": 79.47,
          "en": "Nonetheless, you should know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.47,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "that you technically don't need JSX",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "to build a React project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 86.76,
          "en": "It's just convenient.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.76,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "But you could replace this JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 93.27000000000001,
          "en": "which you might return in a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.27000000000001,
          "end": 98.27000000000001,
          "en": "with this code here, which does not use JSX at all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.72999999999999,
          "end": 103.72999999999999,
          "en": "but which instead only uses standard Java script features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.7,
          "end": 108.6,
          "en": "To be precise, this code snippet on the right here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.6,
          "end": 112.86,
          "en": "uses the createElement method exposed by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.86,
          "end": 115.71000000000001,
          "en": "to create that same structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.71000000000001,
          "end": 119.16,
          "en": "that same HTML code in the end, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 119.16,
          "end": 122.88,
          "en": "as you see on the left without using JSX.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.88,
          "end": 127.88,
          "en": "For that, this createElement method takes the component type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.04,
          "end": 132.21,
          "en": "that should be created, so to say, as the first argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 132.21,
          "end": 134.16,
          "en": "then takes the props object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 134.16,
          "end": 137.55,
          "en": "you might want to pass to that component or element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.55,
          "end": 140.49,
          "en": "And then you can also have child elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.49,
          "end": 144.32999999999998,
          "en": "as the third argument so that you can control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.32999999999998,
          "end": 148.29,
          "en": "which content goes between the opening and closing tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.29,
          "end": 150,
          "en": "of that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150,
          "end": 153.39,
          "en": "And you could go for this non-JSX approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.39,
          "end": 157.89,
          "en": "if you want a project that requires no build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.89,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "because with JSX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 162.84300000000002,
          "en": "you, of course, do need such a build process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 163.8,
          "end": 168.12,
          "en": "But of course, it's not really difficult to create a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.12,
          "end": 171.03,
          "en": "that comes with such a built process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.03,
          "end": 174.54,
          "en": "You don't need to write the code for that process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.54,
          "end": 175.373,
          "en": "on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.373,
          "end": 176.64,
          "en": "And therefore, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.64,
          "end": 180.45,
          "en": "this JSX approach is typically easier to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.45,
          "end": 183.87,
          "en": "and definitely easier to read and understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.87,
          "end": 186.45,
          "en": "because this non-JSX approach, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.45,
          "end": 190.92,
          "en": "is pretty verbose and not necessarily intuitive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.92,
          "end": 193.56,
          "en": "But here in our project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.56,
          "end": 197.01,
          "en": "this project we worked on in the previous section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 197.01,
          "end": 199.77,
          "en": "you'll find my latest code snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.77,
          "end": 202.86,
          "en": "and a link to this project on CodeSandbox",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.86,
          "end": 204.96,
          "en": "attached to this lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.96,
          "end": 207.81,
          "en": "In that project, in the index JSX file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.81,
          "end": 211.14,
          "en": "we could create this app component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.14,
          "end": 216.14,
          "en": "by instead, importing React from react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.6,
          "end": 219.6,
          "en": "So this main React object which is exposed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 221.91,
          "en": "by the React library.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.91,
          "end": 226.23,
          "en": "And instead of creating our root component like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 226.23,
          "end": 230.4,
          "en": "we could create it here by not using JSX",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 230.4,
          "end": 234.46,
          "en": "but by instead calling React, createElement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 235.92000000000002,
          "end": 236.88,
          "en": "and then here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.88,
          "end": 239.91,
          "en": "since we want to use the custom app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.91,
          "end": 242.01,
          "en": "we can just pass a pointer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.01,
          "end": 245.97,
          "en": "at that app component function to createElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.97,
          "end": 250.62,
          "en": "since that's the type of component we want to create here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.62,
          "end": 252.96,
          "en": "And with that, if I would save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 252.96,
          "end": 256.86,
          "en": "I would see the same application as before on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 256.86,
          "end": 259.83,
          "en": "and I also don't get any errors here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.83,
          "end": 264.83,
          "en": "because this here is a valid alternative to this JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 265.23,
          "end": 267.81,
          "en": "But as mentioned, typically you, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 267.81,
          "end": 269.46,
          "en": "go for the JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 269.46,
          "end": 272.61,
          "en": "because it's not really difficult to use here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.61,
          "end": 276.003,
          "en": "and you don't need to manage that build process on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}